      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Specific immunotherapy (SIT) is a common treatment for allergic diseases. Despite its usage in clinical practice for nearly a century, more-rational and safer allergen preparations are required. Here, the underlying mechanisms and principles of allergen modification for the future use of SIT in the treatment of allergy are discussed."},
